If $x,y \in \mathbb{C}^n$, then $\langle x,y \rangle$ denotes the canonical inner product of $x$ and $y$, i.e., 
$$ \langle x,y \rangle = y^\ast x = \sum_{k=1}^n \overline{y_k} \cdot x_k $$ 
and
\[ \begin{Vmatrix} x \end{Vmatrix}_2 \coloneqq \sqrt{\langle x, x \rangle}. \]
