If $n \in \mathbb{N}$, then the \emph{standard (or unit) $n$-simplex}, denoted by $\Delta^n$, is defined by 
\begin{equation*}
\Delta^n = \left\{ (\alpha_1, \dots, \alpha_{n+1}) \in \mathbb{R}^{n+1} \mid \sum_{i=1}^{n+1} \alpha_i =1,~\alpha_i \geqslant 0 \right\}.
\end{equation*}

