        Let $K \subseteq \mathbb{C}^n$ be convex and suppose that $x$ is an extreme point of $K$. If there are vectors $x_1, \dots, x_m \in K$ and a vector $\alpha =[\alpha_1~\cdots~\alpha_m]^\top \in \Delta^{m-1}$ such that $x = \sum_{k=1}^m \alpha_k x_k$, then  $\alpha \in \{ e_1, \dots, e_m \}$.
