codex
The delay exposed a verifier hot path, not a mathematical issue: every rejected random guess was needlessly rescanning all 1,024 target coordinates before checking its first mismatch. I moved the type check into the exact comparison loop, preserving full validation for any candidate that reaches a coordinate while cutting the 200,000-sample audit substantially.
