Step 0 supports the existing direction, with one important correction to the prior triage: “choose a nonnegative matrix and compute its spectrum” would make the answer a routine forward calculation and fails H. The viable family instead uses Theorem 4.29’s exact Walsh spectracone identity. It must be Track B because full Walsh inversion recovers the witness in \(O(n\log n)\), while the intended character-decoding shortcut is much shorter. I found an existing draft in the workspace built around exactly that distinction; I’m auditing it rather than replacing sound work.
